      "side": 1,
      "message": "If my calculations are correct then this changes vm_struct size from 64 bytes into 72 bytes which results in these objects being allocated from the next slab cache of 96 byte objects (see: https://elixir.bootlin.com/linux/latest/source/mm/slab_common.c#L607).\n\nSo we lose 96-64\u003d32 bytes on each vmalloc allocation. Checking /proc/vmallocinfo there are ~10K records there. So if my calculations are right, this one field will cost us ~320K. Are you sure it\u0027s worth it?",
